List<int> countUpTo(int n) {
  List<int> primes = [];
  bool isPrime;
  int i, j;

  for (i = 2; i <= n;) {
    isPrime = true;
    for (j = 0; j < primes.length; j++) {
      if ((primes[j] * primes[j]) <= i || (i % primes[j] != 0)) {
        continue;
      } else {
        isPrime = false;
        break;
      }
    }

    if (isPrime) {
      primes.add(i);
    }

    i++;
  }

  return primes;
}
```

### Explanation:
- The function `countUpTo` generates all prime numbers up to and including `n`.
